# pgstar Extension Development Rules (.cursorrules)

You are an expert PostgreSQL extension + C systems developer working on `pgstar`.
Cursor MUST enforce these rules in every edit.

===============================================================
1. HARD RULES (MANDATORY)
===============================================================

[1] MEMORY SAFETY IS CRITICAL — NEVER BREAK THIS.

- Never return pointers from:
  - SPI context
  - Transaction context
  - Any context that will be freed before the caller returns

- Always deep-copy everything needed by the caller:
  - Strings: pstrdup()
  - bytea/text/varchar (varlena): PG_DETOAST_DATUM_COPY()
  - Buffers: palloc + memcpy()

- All frees MUST use:
    pgstar_safe_pfree(ptr);
  Never call pfree() directly.

- When building API/UI/HTML/JSON responses:
    MemoryContext caller = CurrentMemoryContext;
    Build in Tx memory.
    MemoryContextSwitchTo(caller);
    final = pstrdup(buf.data);
    MemoryContextSwitchTo(old);
    SPI_finish();
    return final;   <-- final now lives in caller's context


===============================================================
2. SPI RULES (STRICT)
===============================================================

[2.1] Preferred pattern ALWAYS:
    bool isnull;
    Datum d = SPI_getbinval(tuple, tupdesc, attnum, &isnull);
    if (!isnull) {
        Oid out_fn;
        bool isvarlena;
        getTypeOutputInfo(atttypid, &out_fn, &isvarlena);
        char *value = OidOutputFunctionCall(out_fn, d);
        use value;
        pgstar_safe_pfree(value);
    }

[2.2] SPI_getvalue() is legacy — AVOID IT. Use SPI_getbinval. If last-resort, then:
  - It MUST wrap the usage in pstrdup() immediately
  - It MUST protect strlen/pstrdup with PG_TRY/PG_CATCH
  - It MUST avoid using the raw pointer in any string op
  - It MUST free the pstrdup’d value with pgstar_safe_pfree()
  - It MUST still check if SPI_getbinval can be used instead; refactor to SPI_getbinval is the preferred solution.

[2.3] Never store SPI pointers in caches, globals, UI, HTTP replies.

[2.4] Cursor must check: Does any pointer used after SPI_finish()
      originate from SPI? If yes → MUST copy it.


===============================================================
3. VARLENA / BINARY RULES
===============================================================

[3.1] For bytea / text / varchar / jsonb (TOAST-able):
  - ALWAYS use:
        bytea *b = (bytea*) PG_DETOAST_DATUM_COPY(datum);
  - Never cast Datum directly to char* or bytea*.

[3.2] Never use strlen() for binary.
  Track explicit length fields.

[3.3] All UI/static assets are stored in TEXT:
  - Raw UTF-8 for text
  - Base64 for binary


===============================================================
4. HTTP & UI RULES
===============================================================

[4.1] PgstarResponse.body must be allocated in caller context.

[4.2] Cursor must verify:
  - resp->body_len is set for binary responses
  - otherwise length = strlen(resp->body)

[4.3] UI cache entries live in TopMemoryContext only.


===============================================================
5. BACKGROUND WORKERS + JOBS
===============================================================

[5.1] Every long loop MUST contain:
    CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS();

[5.2] Error path rules:
  - NEVER call CommitTransactionCommand() inside PG_CATCH
  - ALWAYS call AbortCurrentTransaction()

[5.3] Cursor must ensure ALL SPI sequences follow:
    StartTransactionCommand();
    PushActiveSnapshot(GetTransactionSnapshot());
    SPI_connect();
    ... work ...
    SPI_finish();
    PopActiveSnapshot();
    CommitTransactionCommand();


===============================================================
6. FRONTEND (Vue) RULES
===============================================================

Forbidden in UI:
- <title-bar>
- <window-body>
- <window>

Cursor must remove or rewrite them.


===============================================================
7. MAKEFILE / WORKFLOW RULES
===============================================================

Cursor must never delete or rename:
- make auto
- make log
- make extension-install
- make restart

===============================================================
8. CURSOR CHECKLIST (ALWAYS RUN THROUGH)
===============================================================

[ ] Does any pointer outlive the transaction context?
    → MUST be deep-copied.

[ ] Are any SPI_getvalue() pointers used directly?
    → MUST refactor immediately to a proper SPI_getbinval. The last-resort alternative is to wrap in pstrdup + PG_TRY + safe free, but the target state is to remove SPI_getvalue() entirely.

[ ] Are any varlena values dereferenced?
    → MUST PG_DETOAST_DATUM_COPY.

[ ] Are any StringInfo buffers returned directly?
    → MUST pstrdup() into caller context.

[ ] Are any pfree() calls present?
    → Replace with pgstar_safe_pfree().

[ ] Does any loop lack CHECK_FOR_INTERRUPTS()?
    → Add it.

[ ] Does PG_CATCH wrongly commit?
    → Fix to AbortCurrentTransaction().

[ ] Are HTTP/UI cache entries in TopMemoryContext?
    → Ensure correct context.

===============================================================
END OF FILE
===============================================================
